# Train Flat Dense Single-Mouse 5 FPS Experiment

This workflow trains the same flat Social Attention architecture on extracted
single-mouse samples. Original sequence IDs are split before extraction, so all
three mice from a source sequence stay in the same train or validation split.

## Hypothesis

If the flat model can preserve a single mouse's pose when social context is
removed, pose errors should improve relative to the flat dense triplet
baseline. If pose errors remain high, the weakness is likely in intra-mouse
keypoint modeling rather than inter-mouse interaction.

## Inspect configuration

```sh {"id":"01M24SINGLEMOUSE5FPSCONFIG"}
python src/train.py fit --config src/config/train__flat_dense_single_mouse_5fps.yml --show-config
```

## Train

```sh {"id":"01M24SINGLEMOUSE5FPSTRAIN"}
python src/train.py fit --config src/config/train__flat_dense_single_mouse_5fps.yml --wandb
```

## Benchmark

Run this after training produces
`checkpoints/flat_dense_single_mouse_5fps/flat_best.pt`.

```sh {"id":"01M24SINGLEMOUSE5FPSBENCH"}
python src/benchmark.py --config src/config/benchmark__flat_dense_single_mouse_5fps.yml
```

